      "content": "4. Major Canals & Irrigation Projects"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Yamuna River forms the eastern natural border separating Haryana from Uttar Pradesh.",
        "Karoh Peak in the Morni Hills (Panchkula district) is the highest elevation peak in Haryana at 1,499 meters.",
        "The Western Yamuna Canal is the oldest canal network in Haryana, initially commissioned during the reign of Firoz Shah Tughlaq.",
        "Dhosi Hill, located in Mahendragarh district, is an extinct volcano and prominent site in the Aravalli range in southern Haryana."
      ],
      "id": "z4u8kro"
